## Context

Housekeeping in `chemin-de-voix` failed at 2026-05-12T20:10:23Z with
`error_max_turns` after 41 turns (cap 40). Beat outcome:
`fail/failed`, cost $0.897 (within the per-project `budget_housekeeping`
of $1.08 raised on 2026-05-11).

Why → the agent legitimately had a lot to clean up:
- 3 stale agent worktrees (`agent-a322aaf…`, `agent-a94bda…`,
  `agent-a97182ed…`)
- 5 stale branches (raid-close-tickets, raid-housekeeping,
  update-state, t0123-fix-extraction-failures, t0124-pdf-handler)
- `.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock` not gitignored
- Stale housekeeping branch `claude/housekeeping-20260512T040653Z-ea02`

The agent did most of the cleanup (removed worktrees and branches,
gitignored the lock file, created ticket 0126 in chemin-de-voix), but
ran out of turns while finalising STATE.md and the gitignore commit.

## Why this is recurring

chemin-de-voix housekeeping has failed 5 times since 2026-05-08
(2026-05-08T20:06Z, 2026-05-10T00:07Z, 2026-05-10T03:08Z,
2026-05-11T01:07Z, 2026-05-12T20:10Z). The 2026-05-11 fail was
`error_max_budget_usd` and was repaired by raising `budget_housekeeping`
to $1.08 in `~/.claude/beat.json`. With budget no longer binding,
max_turns is now the binding constraint.

`scripts/beat.py` exposes `max_turns_pick_ticket` per-project on
`ProjectConfig` but uses the module-level `MAX_TURNS_HOUSEKEEPING = 40`
unconditionally at the housekeeping call site (beat.py:790). Supervisor
authority says "raise the per-project ProjectConfig field by 20%, capped
at 2× module-level". There is no per-project field for housekeeping —
adding one is outside auto-repair authority.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Add `max_turns_housekeeping: int = MAX_TURNS_HOUSEKEEPING` to
      `ProjectConfig` in `scripts/beat.py`.
- [ ] Wire it through to the housekeeping `_run_skill` call site
      (beat.py:790) alongside the existing `max_turns_pick_ticket`
      pattern.
- [ ] Add `"max_turns_housekeeping"` to the per-project allowlist
      (around `scripts/beat.py:154`).
- [ ] Set `max_turns_housekeeping: 48` for `chemin-de-voix` (40 × 1.2)
      in `scripts/beat-settings.json`.
- [ ] Once merged, supervisor can apply the standard 20% bump rule when
      housekeeping hits max_turns repeatedly on any project.

## Notes for implementer

- Module-level `MAX_TURNS_HOUSEKEEPING` must not change.
- Cap the per-project value at `2 * MAX_TURNS_HOUSEKEEPING = 80` per the
  supervisor authority rule.
- Re-check chemin-de-voix repo state before bumping — if the same
  worktree/branch sludge re-accumulates, the upstream fix is whatever
  raid/sweep is leaving cruft behind, not a higher housekeeping cap.
